   ✋ ConstraintError: KEY FINGERPRINT MISMATCH — <fixture>/key.gpg
      expected exactly these primary key(s):
        AAAA1111BBBB2222CCCC3333DDDD4444EEEE5555
      received:
        FFFF9999FFFF9999FFFF9999FFFF9999FFFF9999
      ⇒ do NOT install this key. it is the trust anchor for every
        package apt will take from that source, so a wrong key here is
        not one bad install — it is every future one, each with a clean
        signature check against the wrong anchor
      ⇒ an EXTRA key is as bad as a wrong one: the pin is a set, so a
        keyring holding the right key plus another still fails, and
        that is deliberate
      ⇒ if upstream genuinely rotated, source the new fingerprint from
        their published documentation — never from the download you are
        trying to verify
